---
import BaseLayout from "../../site/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../../site/styles/mobile-menu-study.css";
---

<BaseLayout title="Mobile menu study — Mourne Made" description="A visual study of the mobile menu for Mourne Made." hideFooter>
  <main class="mobile-menu-study">
    <div class="shell mobile-menu-study-intro">
      <a class="mobile-menu-study-back" href="/prototypes/field-study/">← Field study</a>
      <p class="home-kicker">Mourne Made · component study</p>
      <h1>How should the menu open?</h1>
      <p class="mobile-menu-study-lede">Three mobile menu treatments, shown at the size they’ll actually be used. The navigation stays simple; the question is how much surface it needs.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="shell mobile-menu-study-grid">
      <article class="mobile-option"><p class="mobile-option-name"><span>A</span> Ink panel</p><div class="mobile-demo mobile-demo--ink"><button>Close</button><nav><a href="#">Transformations</a><a href="#">Why local</a><a href="#">Free before-and-after</a></nav></div><p>Current direction: a compact dark panel gives the open state strong contrast.</p></article>
      <article class="mobile-option"><p class="mobile-option-name"><span>B</span> Blue panel</p><div class="mobile-demo mobile-demo--blue"><button>Close</button><nav><a href="#">Transformations</a><a href="#">Why local</a><a href="#">Free before-and-after</a></nav></div><p>Uses the approved blue as the menu surface and keeps the CTA yellow.</p></article>
      <article class="mobile-option"><p class="mobile-option-name"><span>C</span> Open sheet</p><div class="mobile-demo mobile-demo--sheet"><button>Close</button><nav><a href="#">Transformations</a><a href="#">Why local</a><a href="#">Free before-and-after</a></nav></div><p>Turns the menu into a full-width sheet, giving each action more breathing room.</p></article>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
